########################## Process of creating Python Virtual Environment ##########################

python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate



########################## Process of creating requirements.txt and installing the packages ##########################

Create requirements.txt file
pip install -r requirements.txt
deactivate ---> just write to deactivate


To install a package :
pip install <package-name>

To delete an installed package :
pip uninstall <package-name>



########################## Pushing a new file to GitHub ##########################
git init

** Create a .gitignore file. Inside .gitignore file place .venv/ and __pycache__/

git add .

git commit -m "Initial commit"

git remote add origin https://github.com/YourUsername/YourRepo.git

git branch -M <branch-name>



########################## Making changes and pushing it in Github ##########################

Do not start commanding from venv.

git add .

git commit -m "Commit what changes are done."

git push origin <Branch-name>



########################## Downloading project from GitHub using command ##########################
Make sure to navigate the terminal to the folder where you want to clone the project.

git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/YOUR-REPO-NAME.git .

git checkout AI-Chatbot
